  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor having plates of area <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> and plate separation <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> , has capacitance <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> in air. When two dielectrics of different relative permittivities ( <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> ) are introduced between the two plates as shown in the figure, the capacitance becomes <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_8fdee2670d86.jpg\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
